.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MKNOD 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mknod
.Nd make device special files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar name
.Nm
.Ar name
.Cm b | c
.Ar major minor
.Op Ar owner : Ns Ar group
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes
.Ar name ,
a block
.Pq Cm b
or character
.Pq Cm c
special file for the device numbered
.Ar major
and
.Ar minor ,
with mode 0666 less the
.Xr umask 2 .
The numbers are read as
.Xr strtoul 3
reads them: a leading
.Ql 0x
means hexadecimal, a leading
.Ql 0
octal.
.Pp
With
.Ar owner : Ns Ar group ,
both given, as names or numbers (a name that is also a number counts as a
name), the file is given to them.
.Pp
With only a
.Ar name ,
.Nm
asks for a character special file of device 0, which in
.Xr devfs 4
recreates a node that was removed, where the file system allows it.
.Pp
Device nodes normally come from
.Xr devfs 4 ,
under
.Pa /dev ;
nodes made elsewhere are files that name a device by number.
FIFOs are made with
.Xr mkfifo 1 .
Only the superuser may make device special files.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl mknod /tmp/null c 1 3 root:wheel
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mkfifo 1 ,
.Xr mknod 2 ,
.Xr devfs 4 ,
.Xr chown 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v6 .
